{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Entreat YHWH.</b> He mentioned the honored Name and said \"the voice of Elohim,\" for he acknowledges that there is Elohim, as I have mentioned. And because he did not say \"the voice of YHWH,\" Moses joined the noun of substance and the attribute and said, \"because of YHWH Elohim\" (Exodus 9:30). The sense is that the Name — He alone is Elohim. You will not find thus in the words of Moses in all the Torah. And there is no objection from the verse \"Lord YHWH, You have begun\" (Deuteronomy 3:24), for it is written with alef-dalet [i.e., Adonai, not the independent word 'Lord' meaning 'master']."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :register {:flags {0 ["Lord"]}}, :notes {0 "The closing citation reads ד' אלהים אתה החלות; the first word is the abbreviation ד׳ for Adonai, which he clarifies is written with alef-dalet (אדני), not a separate noun 'master.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:03.888646007Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}